    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-koto-wa-ga",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Reduplication frame, not a single linear derivation. The formation field repeats the SAME predicate on both sides of ことは (verb + ことは + verb + が; i-adjective + ことは + i-adjective + が; na-adjective + な + ことは + na-adjective + だが; noun + ことは + noun + だが). An ordered step list transforms one base and then suffixes FIXED tokens, so the second copy of the host word cannot be emitted: any token placed in append would hard-code one specific word and re-emit it for every other base. Steps covering only the first half would license 書くことは as if it were the whole pattern. Note also that structure_pattern and forms[0].form on this record both carry an unapplied edit instruction instead of a value, so the intended shape ～ことは～が had to be read out of the formation prose.",
      "nuance_tags": ["concession", "softening"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
