    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-kurai-wa-nai",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Two-slot frame. The formation field defines it as host + くらい + は followed by a SEPARATE negative predicate (or by 〜ないと), as in 週に一度くらいはジムに行かないと. The closed op set builds one base and suffixes tokens to it, so it can reach 一度くらいは but has no way to bind the second, independent predicate slot that carries the obligatory negation, and that negation is what produces the at-least-this-minimum reading. Emitting only the くらいは half would license 一度くらいは as if it were the complete construction. Note also that structure_pattern and forms[0].form on this record both carry an unapplied edit instruction instead of a value; the intended shape ～くらいは～ない was read out of the formation prose.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis", "obligation"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "casual-friends"]
